From 0098ba2ba0919487d9f5f70252845345dacd3a47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:14:39 -0800
Subject: PM: runtime: Only queue an idle check for RPM-linked suppliers (part
 2)

From: Brian Norris <briannorris@chromium.org>

[ Upstream commit bd56424ce808fb1f92a4dc5bdeedc45b85c5d6cd ]

Commit be5755f023e7 ("PM: runtime: Only queue an idle check for
RPM-linked suppliers") was incomplete. There are two other cases where
we perform idle checks on non-DL_FLAG_PM_RUNTIME suppliers -- in
pm_runtime_set_suspended(), and in cases where we failed to resume
suppliers.

Fixes: be5755f023e7 ("PM: runtime: Only queue an idle check for RPM-linked suppliers")
Fixes: 5244f5e2d801 ("PM: runtime: Defer suspending suppliers")
Signed-off-by: Brian Norris <briannorris@chromium.org>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261103141442.v2.1.If69ddc515c2e9fd4338441e87688b9d690d2ef36@changeid
Signed-off-by: Rafael J. Wysocki <rafael.j.wysocki@intel.com>
[ sashal: Replaced the missing device_link_test() helper with the open-coded link->flags & DL_FLAG_PM_RUNTIME test in __rpm_put_suppliers(). ]
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
---
 drivers/base/power/runtime.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/base/power/runtime.c b/drivers/base/power/runtime.c
index cf128d062f072..fd02b8a206b2d 100644
--- a/drivers/base/power/runtime.c
+++ b/drivers/base/power/runtime.c
@@ -329,6 +329,9 @@ static void __rpm_put_suppliers(struct device *dev, bool try_to_suspend)
 
 	list_for_each_entry_rcu(link, &dev->links.suppliers, c_node,
 				device_links_read_lock_held()) {
+		if (!(link->flags & DL_FLAG_PM_RUNTIME))
+			continue;
+
 		pm_runtime_release_supplier(link);
 		if (try_to_suspend)
 			pm_request_idle(link->supplier);
-- 
